.TH LAZYCONTEINER 1 "November 2026" "LazyConteiner" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lazyconteiner \- native desktop interface for local Docker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lazyconteiner
.RB [ --demo | --smoke-test | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts the native Exact UI and an authenticated loopback Docker bridge as the
current desktop user. The bridge stops when the window closes. Closing the
application does not stop Docker containers.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --demo
Use isolated sample data without accessing Docker.
.TP
.B --smoke-test
Check packaged executables and the authenticated demo bridge without opening a window.
.TP
.B --version
Print the installed application version.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/lazyconteiner/config.json
stores project paths, terminal settings and custom commands. XDG_CONFIG_HOME
overrides the default directory.
.PP
.I ~/.local/state/lazyconteiner/
contains private backend.log and ui.log files. XDG_STATE_HOME overrides this path.
.SH NOTES
Run without sudo. Docker access must already be configured for the current user.
Only local Unix Docker sockets are supported. Compose and interactive terminal
operations require the Docker CLI, Compose plugin and a terminal emulator.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR docker (1),
.BR apt (8)
